## 3. `mcp` in isolated runtime environments

All three runtime locks use the same security-fixed version:

| Component | Version | License | Why this version |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `index-service` | 1.28.1 | MIT | Exact direct pin and complete runtime lock; includes the fixes listed above. |
| `agent-container` | 1.28.1 | MIT | Locked transitive dependency, compatible with `claude-agent-sdk==0.2.103` and the OpenAI Agents SDK. |
| `glossary worker` | 1.28.1 | MIT | Locked transitive dependency in `index-service/glossary-requirements.lock`. |

The environments remain separate: `index-service` runs on the EC2 index host,
`agent-container` runs in the AgentCore microVM, and the glossary worker uses
its own interpreter. The agent and index-service communicate over HTTP.
Changes to the index client require CodeGraph protocol verification;
runtime dependency changes must regenerate the corresponding locks.

`uvicorn` still ships at 0.44.0 (index-service, pinned)
and 0.49.0 (agent-container, transitive).

